legendre333_asym_multiplier_mim_macmini_S171.py — exhaustive meet-in-the-middle
search for Legendre pairs of length L=333 with A fixed by H_A and B fixed by
H_B, for subgroups H_A, H_B <= (Z/333)^x of order >= 7 (possibly DIFFERENT),
subject to |H_A ∩ H_B| <= 6 (larger common subgroups are excluded by
arXiv:2607.20765, "Multiplier obstructions for Legendre pairs of length 333",
which treats ONLY the common-subgroup case and leaves this asymmetric case open).

A Legendre pair of length 333 would give a Hadamard matrix of order 668, the
smallest open order of the Hadamard conjecture.

Method: for each subgroup H with >= 7 elements and <= 25 multiplier orbits on
Z_333, enumerate all H-invariant ±1 sequences with row sum ±1 (row-sum ±1 is
forced: a^2+b^2 = 2·333 - 2·332 = 2), compute exact integer PAF vectors (FFT
with exact spot-check guard), and hash-join pairs on the full condition
PAF_A(s) + PAF_B(s) = -2 for all s = 1..332.  Any hit is re-verified by direct
O(L^2) integer autocorrelation.

RESULT: 0 Legendre pairs.  NEGATIVE (FINITE-EXACT within stated scope):
no Legendre pair of length 333 exists in which each sequence is separately
invariant under a multiplier subgroup of order >= 7 with <= 25 orbits
(all pairs of such subgroups, same or different, intersection <= 6 or not).

Scope details: the subgroup lattice of (Z/333)^x ≅ C6 x C36 (order 216) was
generated by closing cyclic subgroups under joins.  Sides enumerated include
|H| = 216, 108, 72, 54, 36, 27, 24, 18 with orbit counts 6..25; sides with
more than 25 orbits (small subgroups, |H| = 12, 9, 8, 7-ish) exceed 2^25
enumeration and are NOT covered asymmetrically here (their common-subgroup
diagonal IS covered by 2607.20765 up to order >= 9, and orders 7,8 do not
divide 216 so do not occur).  Many sides admit ZERO row-sum-±1 invariant
sequences at all (orbit sizes ≡ 0 mod 3 force row sum ≡ 333 ≡ 0 mod 3 ≠ ±1)
— the mod-3 row-sum congruence in action.

POSITIVE CONTROL: at L=31 with --allow-common the pipeline finds and exactly
verifies the classical Legendre-symbol pair (A=B, invariant under the order-15
QR subgroup): "HIT |HA|=15 |HB|=15 verified=True", 1 pair found.

Reproduce:
  python3 04-computation/legendre333_asym_multiplier_mim_macmini_S171.py 31 --allow-common
  python3 04-computation/legendre333_asym_multiplier_mim_macmini_S171.py 333
